  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Combined Workers and Hidden Individual Rates",
    "description": "Find an unknown worker or helper by subtracting known work rates.",
    "teachingApproach": "Make the hidden-rate idea visual: the team's rate is the sum of its members, so a missing member is team minus known member. Build from two workers to a third helper, partial-work clues, and staged remainder clues. Keep every unknown as a daily rate until the final reciprocal converts it into days.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 29,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 17, Time and Work. Approved scope: Teach subtraction of work rates: if A+B have a known rate and B is known, then A is the difference. Extend to a third helper, one known pair plus an individual, partial-work clues that reveal an individual's whole-job time, and questions where a worker completes the remainder after another has worked first. Keep the unknown as a rate before converting it back into days."
  },
